<article class="env-lemma" id="09PW">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/09PW">Lemma <span data-tag="09PW">23.7.5</span>.</a> Let $(A, \mathfrak m)$ be a Noetherian local ring. Let $I \subset J \subset A$ be proper ideals. Assume </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$A/J$ has finite tor dimension over $A/I$, and 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$J$ is generated by a regular sequence. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
  <p> Then $I$ is generated by a regular sequence and $J/I$ is generated by a regular sequence. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      By Lemma <a href="/tag/09PV" data-tag="09PV">23.7.4</a> we see that $I/\mathfrak m I \to J/\mathfrak m J$ is injective. Thus we can find $s \leq r$ and a minimal system of generators $f_1, \ldots , f_ r$ of $J$ such that $f_1, \ldots , f_ s$ are in $I$ and form a minimal system of generators of $I$. The lemma follows as any minimal system of generators of $J$ is a regular sequence by More on Algebra, Lemmas <a href="/tag/066A" data-tag="066A">15.31.15</a> and <a href="/tag/09CC" data-tag="09CC">15.31.7</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>